;; signal.sigwaitinfo, signal.sigtimedwait and signal.struct_siginfo (queue 242, :siginfo; Modules/signalmodule.c's
;; fill_siginfo and signal_sigwaitinfo_impl, signal_sigtimedwait_impl). Go's handlers give no siginfo_t, so the sender
;; is recorded where pyi knows it: kill and pthread_kill of the own process (SI_USER with the own pid and uid, SI_TKILL),
;; the interval timers (SI_KERNEL); a signal that comes from another process is reported as SI_USER from pid 0 and uid 0
;; (the divergence :siginfo keeps). The first arrival of a signal that is already held or pending keeps its record, as
;; the kernel keeps the first instance of a standard signal.

